.TH CW "1" "October 2026" "cw 0.1.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
cw \- cw create
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B cw
\fI\,create \/\fR[\fI\,OPTIONS\/\fR] \fI\,NAME\/\fR
.SH DESCRIPTION
.IP
Create a new Context.
.IP
By default creates an empty Context. Use \fB\-a\fR to also add the current window.
.IP
Examples:
.TP
cw create MyProject
empty Context
.TP
cw create MyProject \fB\-a\fR
create + add current window
.IP
cw create MyProject \fB\-a\fR \fB\-d\fR "Frontend dev"
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-d\fR, \fB\-\-description\fR TEXT
Optional description for the Context.
.TP
\fB\-a\fR, \fB\-\-add\fR
Also add the current window to the new Context.
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Show this message and exit.
